                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "02fe2af6-7572-4b92-8344-8fbbc22f274d",
                        "source_entry_id": "3e835ad0-512f-39ab-9b5e-4c5a12ec1110",
                        "source_sense_id": "1401f68b-fc61-382f-9935-631b24106df5",
                        "source_sense_description": "Laubbaum der biologischen Gattung Salix; Weide",
                        "target_lang_word": "willow",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "willow",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "abf78075-0c11-3665-a20b-b2160c13f188",
                                        "entry_id": "6fa10b07-ffb2-3dfe-affa-c21adf425347",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various deciduous trees or shrubs in the genus Salix, in the willow family Salicaceae, found primarily on moist soils in cooler zones in the northern hemisphere."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d63059e3-e2cf-4245-9c8b-3d08abdbbaf6",
                                                "sense_id": "abf78075-0c11-3665-a20b-b2160c13f188",
                                                "text": "[…] and through the middle of this forest, from wall to wall, ran a winding line of brilliant green which marked the course of cottonwoods and willows."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1451d451-6d97-4d53-aca4-15b2a255a8f8",
                                                "sense_id": "abf78075-0c11-3665-a20b-b2160c13f188",
                                                "text": "And willows, willow-herb, and grass, / And meadowsweet, and haycocks dry, / No whit less still and lonely fair / Than the high cloudlets in the sky."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e89b5ada-a379-4fc3-8010-116724845a0a",
                                                "sense_id": "abf78075-0c11-3665-a20b-b2160c13f188",
                                                "text": "The pounded leaves of the willow, drunk in a concoction, were formerly reputed to diminish amatory desires."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db242afd-3d5b-41f7-83bd-1a1cc8c10c15",
                                                "sense_id": "abf78075-0c11-3665-a20b-b2160c13f188",
                                                "text": "By old age she was emaciated, the bones jutting out of her face and her figure frail as a willow branch."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b81b37d-5851-3bcf-849e-8e832b3afaf5",
                                        "entry_id": "6fa10b07-ffb2-3dfe-affa-c21adf425347",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The wood of these trees."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "35c4fff4-bd33-3bb2-8f0c-c4444caab2a4",
                                        "entry_id": "6fa10b07-ffb2-3dfe-affa-c21adf425347",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cricket bat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a64fcb82-aa4d-3858-a469-8276d8e67fd8",
                                        "entry_id": "6fa10b07-ffb2-3dfe-affa-c21adf425347",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The baseball bat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e520e98-d12f-30ec-974b-dcf1560d70fc",
                                        "entry_id": "6fa10b07-ffb2-3dfe-affa-c21adf425347",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rotating spiked drum used to open and clean cotton heads."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "willow",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4406e0d1-c15d-3005-bce9-dfbea67ccbbf",
                                        "entry_id": "eeb16f57-86e7-34fc-acad-71194ebb75d0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To open and cleanse (cotton, flax, wool, etc.) by means of a willow."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cebbb950-10d0-39be-a6bd-ecc5ceec0398",
                                        "entry_id": "eeb16f57-86e7-34fc-acad-71194ebb75d0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To form a shape or move in a way similar to the long, slender branches of a willow."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3e57fcf-d0e8-447e-b34a-a1ad35e87be1",
                                                "sense_id": "cebbb950-10d0-39be-a6bd-ecc5ceec0398",
                                                "text": "Willowing over the rough cobbles of the little pier stepped a thin, bent figure, adorned with a silver nanny-goat's beard and bobbling eyes interrupted by the rim of a pair of pince-nez."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0efe361b-28ef-43bb-adad-956a9ca5b64e",
                                                "sense_id": "cebbb950-10d0-39be-a6bd-ecc5ceec0398",
                                                "text": "Joe’s impulse was to sketch her, with her shadow willowing beyond her on the mouse-gray paving-stone; but his left fist, obeying instinct, remained clenched behind his back […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33d74321-d34f-41b8-8113-946abf2bea9a",
                                                "sense_id": "cebbb950-10d0-39be-a6bd-ecc5ceec0398",
                                                "text": "It was floating a foot under the surface. The eyes were holes. The mouth was a slit cavern of darkness. The hair willowed around the scalp."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c34118ea-2e2d-43b7-94c8-650f4b8d391b",
                                                "sense_id": "cebbb950-10d0-39be-a6bd-ecc5ceec0398",
                                                "text": "The draft-drawn smoke willowed down through the hole and across my face, but I didn’t worry about coughing or sneezing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "778696cc-9638-42e5-9187-69c16a142ca4",
                        "source_entry_id": "3e835ad0-512f-39ab-9b5e-4c5a12ec1110",
